      'OpenCLI\'s useful idea is determinism: instead of asking an LLM to guess at a page, it turns websites and browser sessions into commands with stable JSON output. Commands return {ok, data} or a structured error with a code, message and hint, logs go to stderr, and capability discovery is paginated. That gives an agent a reliable contract to call. It ships built-in adapters for sites such as Bilibili, Zhihu, Xiaohongshu, Reddit, Hacker News and X, plus a general browser mode for any page through your logged-in Chrome profile. The trade-off is that it is infrastructure for agents rather than an agent itself, and the README notes a breaking change to CLI syntax and JSON output that users of older versions need to account for.',
